;; LOCALLY-MINTED messages: shapes this generator declares itself, which no
;; descriptor database carries.
;;
;; A MINT DECLARES NO FIELD NUMBER, AND THE SCHEMA HAS NO KEY FOR ONE. That is
;; what leaves `numbering-registry.edn` as the only possible source of a number
;; — the generator refuses to run against an unpinned field rather than
;; inventing one, so a number here cannot move because a policy changed.
{"pgfix.Heartbeat"
 {:name "Heartbeat"
  :fields [{:name "seq" :type :uint32 :constraints {:gte 1}}
           {:name "sent_at_ns" :type :uint64}]}}
